    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18626" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Achaean,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, etc.: hence as Subst., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιοί, οἱ,</span>
			<i>the Achaeans,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> for the <u>Greeks</u> generally, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.235
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαΐα</span></b> , ἡ, <u>Achaia</u> in Peloponnese, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
			</span></i>, etc.; under the Romans, <i>the province of
		Greece.</i></div>
